# "Free movement" and "Move while aiming" (DevJunior's mod in the spirit of the 2023 remake; the app menu's
# Controls page, both off by default): runtime/free_move.cpp. cPlayer::keyConfig calls re4_player_input first,
# before the walk routines read the keys: with "Free movement" the main stick turns Leon toward where it points,
# seen from the camera, and the game gets only "forward" (its walk and run do the rest); the C stick turns the
# camera round him, R3 brings it back behind him. With "Move while aiming" the C stick walks him while a weapon or
# the knife is ready; cPlayer::move calls re4_player_after_routine after the routines, which puts his walk motion
# on his legs meanwhile. CameraQuasiFPS::calcBaseMatrix asks re4_free_cam_matrix to turn the camera's base frame
# to the free camera's yaw (only in the walk routines, and on the way back behind him after them). Both off:
# nothing changes.
